.TH LIBUTF8_DECODE_MEM 3 LIBUTF8
.SH NAME
libutf8_decode_mem - Decode one UTF-8 sequence from a memory buffer

.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <libutf8.h>

size_t \fBlibutf8_decode_mem\fP(const char *\fItext\fP, size_t \fItext_len\fP, uint_least32_t *\fIcodepoint_out\fP, unsigned \fIflags\fP);
.fi
.PP
Link with
.IR -lutf8 .

.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.BR libutf8_decode_mem ()
function decodes the first UTF-8 sequence in
.IR text ,
however it the sequence is longer than
.I text_len
it reads the first byte and returns the
sequence length indicated by that byte. In
this case it is unspecified whether it reads
any other byte than the first byte.

Unless the
.BR libutf8_decode_mem ()
function returns 0 or a value greater than
.IR text_len ,
and unless
.I codepoint_out
is
.IR NULL ,
the decoded codepoint is stored in
.IR *codepoint_out .
.PP
.I flags
is a bitwise OR of zero or more of the following values:
.TP
.B LIBUTF8_REPLACE_INVALID
Replace decoded invalid codepoints up to
.B LIBUTF8_ULTIMATE_CODEPOINT
with the Unicode REPLACEMENT CHARACTER (U+FFFD).
This does not affect illegal byte sequences.
.TP
.B LIBUTF8_RETURN_INVALID
Return decoded invalid codepoints up to
.B LIBUTF8_ULTIMATE_CODEPOINT
unchanged.
.TP
.B LIBUTF8_ALLOW_31_BITS
Accept codepoints greater than
.BR LIBUTF8_ULTIMATE_CODEPOINT ,
up to representable with 31 bits, unsigned.
.TP
.B LIBUTF8_ALLOW_2BYTE_NULL
Accept the two-byte overlong encoding of U+0000.
.TP
.B LIBUTF8_ALLOW_LONG_ENCODING
Accept overlong encodings up to six bytes.
This includes the encoding accepted by
.BR LIBUTF8_ALLOW_2BYTE_NULL .
.PP
It is unspecified which flag dominates if both
.B LIBUTF8_REPLACE_INVALID
and
.B LIBUTF8_RETURN_INVALID
are set.

.SH RETURN VALUE
The
.BR libutf8_decode_mem ()
function returns the number of decoded bytes,
or zero if the input is invalid. However if
the sequence is longer than
.I text_len
is returns the indicated sequence length.
.PP
It is unspecified which is returned, 0 or
the indicated sequence length when the leading
byte indicates a length longer than
.I text_len
but the other available bytes do not create
a valid continuation.

.SH ERRORS
The function cannot fail per se, and never sets
.IR errno .
.B EILSEQ
is an appropriate value when it returns zero.

.SH ATTRIBUTES
For an explanation of the terms used in this section, see
.BR attributes (7).
.PP
.TS
allbox;
lb lb lb lb
l l l l.
Interface	Thread safety	Async-signal safety	Async-cancel safety
T{
.BR libutf8_decode_mem ()
T}	MT-Safe	AS-Safe	AC-Safe
.TE
.sp

.SH APPLICATION USAGE
Application that use
.BR LIBUTF8_REPLACE_INVALID (3)
will probably also want to skip the first
undecoded by when 0 is returned and insert
.BR LIBUTF8_REPLACEMENT_CHARACTER_CODEPOINT (3)
in its place, and optionally skip the following
bytes until there is one for which
.BR libutf8_is_continuation (3)
returns zero.

